 body
  h1 Crochet pattern for a dragon
  p Dragon amigurumi pattern
  blockquote
    p This little dragon is a playful, pocket-sized project with a round body, tiny wings, and a gentle smile. It is great for a first larger amigurumi piece if you like simple shaping and a little bit of embroidery.
    p The finished toy is cuddly, bright, and easy to customize with your favorite yarn colors.
  p #[a(href="https://www.ravelry.com/" ) Reference inspiration]
  h2 Pattern: Dragon
  p
  | This pattern uses basic stitches and a soft worsted yarn. The body is worked in one piece, with simple ears, wings, and tail added after.
  h3 Head
  ul
    li R1: MR, 6 sc into ring (6 sts)
    li R2: Inc in each st around (12 sts)
    li R3: [Sc 1, inc] repeat around (18 sts)
    li R4: [Sc 2, inc] repeat around (24 sts)
    li R5: [Sc 3, inc] repeat around (30 sts)
    li R6: [Sc 4, inc] repeat around (36 sts)
    li R7: [Sc 5, inc] repeat around (42 sts)
    li R8: [Sc 6, inc] repeat around (48 sts)
    li R9-R16: Sc in each st around (48 sts) for 8 rounds
    li R17: [Sc 6, dec] repeat around (42 sts)
    li R18: [Sc 5, dec] repeat around (36 sts)
  p Insert safety eyes between R12 and R13, approximately 10 stitches apart. The holographic rainbow eyes really bring this dragon to life, so take your time positioning them.
  ul
    li R19: [Sc 4, dec] repeat around (30 sts)
    li R20: [Sc 3, dec] repeat around (24 sts)
  p Begin stuffing firmly. You want the head nice and round.
  ul
    li R21: [Sc 2, dec] repeat around (18 sts)
  p Continue stuffing as you close.
  ul
    li R22: [Sc 1, dec] repeat around (12 sts)
    li R23: Dec around (6 sts)
  p FO, leaving a long tail. Close the hole by weaving through the front loops of remaining stitches and pulling tight.
  h3 Snout
  ul
    li R1: MR, 6 sc into ring (6 sts)
    li R2: Inc in each st around (12 sts)
    li R3: [Sc 1, inc] repeat around (18 sts)
    li R4: [Sc 2, inc] repeat around (24 sts)
    li R5: [Sc 3, inc] repeat around (30 sts)
    li R6: [Sc 4, inc] repeat around (36 sts)
    li R7-R11: Sc in each st around (36 sts) for 5 rounds
    li R12: [Sc 4, dec] repeat around (30 sts)
    li R13: [Sc 3, dec] repeat around (24 sts)
  h4 Nose Detail
  ol
    li sl st into first marked st on R5, 2 hdc into next 3 sts, sl st into last marked st on R5 [8]
  img(src="./snout-nose-patern.jpg" title="Crochet snout nose detail" alt="Diagram showing how to crochet a nose detail onto the dragon snout")
  h3 Arms (Make 2)
  ul
    li R1: With MC, make a magic ring, 6 sc into ring. (6 sts)
    li R2: Inc in each st around. (12 sts)
    li R3-R5: Sc in each st around. (12 sts)
    li R6: Sc 1, invdec repeat around. (8 sts)
    li R7-R12: Sc in each st around. (8 sts)
  h3 Body
  ul
    li R1: With MC, make a magic ring, 6 sc into ring. (6 sts)
    li R2: Inc in each st around. (12 sts)
    li R3: Sc 1, inc repeat around. (18 sts)
    li R4: Sc 2, inc repeat around. (24 sts)
    li R5: Sc 3, inc repeat around. (30 sts)
    li R6: Sc 4, inc repeat around. (36 sts)
    li R7-R14: Sc in each st around. (36 sts) - 8 rounds even
    li R15: Sc 4, invdec repeat around. (30 sts)
    li R16-R18: Sc in each st around. (30 sts)
    li R19: Sc 3, invdec repeat around. (24 sts) Attach one arm on each side as you work this round.
    li R20-R22: Sc in each st around. (24 sts)
  h3 Feet (Make Two)
  ul
    li R1: Using Colour A, make a MC and SC 8 into the MC. (8)
    li R2: (SCINC) x 2, SC 2, (SCINC) x 2, SC 2. (12)
    li R3: SC around. (12)
    li R4: SCINC, SC, SCINC, SC 3, SCINC, SC, SCINC, SC 3. (16)
    li R5-R9: SC around. (16)
    li R10: (SCDEC) x 3, SC 10. (13)
    li R11: (SCDEC) x 3, SC 7. (10) - Add stuffing to the foot. Stuff firmly. Do not add any more stuffing to the foot beyond this point.
    li R12-R16: SC around. (10)
    li R17: (SCDEC) x 5. (5)
  h3 Tail
  ul
    li R1: MR, 4 sc
    li R2: 1 sc, inc, 1 sc, inc
    li R3: 3 sc, inc, 2 sc (7)
    li R4: 3 sc, inc, 3 sc (8)
    li R5: 2 sc, inc, 2 sc, inc, 2 sc (10)
    li R6: 3 sc, inc, 2 sc, inc, 3 sc (12)
    li R7: 3 sc, inc, sc, inc, sc, inc, 4 sc (15)
    li R8: 3 sc, inc, 3 sc, inc, 3 sc, inc, 3 sc (18)
    li R9: 4 sc, inc, 3 sc, inc, 3 sc, inc, 5 sc (21)
    li R10: 21 sc
    li R11: 5 sc, inc, 4 sc, inc, 4 sc, inc, 5 sc (24)
    li R12: 5 sc, inc, 4 sc, inc, 2 sc, inc, 4 sc, inc, 5 sc (28)
    li R13: 5 sc, inc, 5 sc, inc, 4 sc, inc, 5 sc, inc, 5 sc (32)
    li R14: 4 sc, inc, 8 sc, inc, 4 sc, inc, 8 sc, inc, 4 sc (36)
    li R15: 11 sc, inc, 4 sc, inc, 2 sc, inc, 4 sc, inc, 11 sc (40)
    li R16: 40 sc
    li R17: 6 sc, dec, 8 sc, dec, 4 sc, dec, 8 sc, dec, 6 sc (36)
    li R18: 40 sc
    li R19: 40 sc
  